"<p>Nitrobase exposes a team-scoped REST API at <code>/api/v1</code> and a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server at <code>/api/mcp</code>. Both use the same bearer API tokens prefixed with <code>nbk_</code>.</p>\n<h2>Creating an API Token</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Settings → API tokens</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create token</strong> (personal tokens act within your permissions; team tokens require <code>tokens.manage</code>).</li>\n<li>Pick a <strong>Preset</strong> or select individual permissions, and set an expiration (maximum lifetime <code>API_TOKEN_MAX_TTL_DAYS</code>, default <code>365</code> days):\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Read-only:</strong> Lists servers, apps, jobs, backups, and metrics; changes nothing.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployer (CI):</strong> <code>app.deploy</code> (plus implied views) — deploys, redeploys, restarts apps, and follows jobs.</li>\n<li><strong>Backups operator:</strong> <code>backup.create</code> (plus implied views) — triggers and lists backups.</li>\n<li><strong>Admin:</strong> All team permissions you hold.</li>\n<li><strong>AI agent (read-only):</strong> <code>server.view</code>, <code>app.view</code>, <code>backup.view</code>, <code>monitoring.view</code> — every read-only MCP tool except <code>preflight_app</code> (which requires <code>app.deploy</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>AI agent (operator):</strong> Read-only agent permissions plus <code>app.deploy</code> and <code>backup.create</code> — reads everything, creates, deploys, starts, stops, restarts, and backs up apps.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Copy the generated token (<code>nbk_...</code>). Tokens are shown <strong>once</strong> and stored only as a cryptographic hash.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Authenticating Requests</h2>\n<p>Send the token in the <code>Authorization</code> header:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">curl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -H</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"Authorization: Bearer nbk_your_token_here\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">  https://panel.example.com/api/v1/apps</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>Rate Limiting &#x26; Auditing</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rate limit:</strong> <code>120</code> requests per minute per token (or per client IP before auth), configurable via <code>API_RATE_LIMIT</code> and <code>API_RATE_WINDOW_MS</code>. Exceeding the limit returns HTTP <code>429</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Audit log:</strong> Every REST and MCP call is recorded in the team's audit log (MCP calls are tagged <code>channel: mcp</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Status codes:</strong> <code>401</code> (missing, invalid, revoked, or expired token), <code>403</code> (token lacks required permission), <code>404</code> (resource not found in token's team), <code>429</code> (rate limited).</li>\n</ul>"